title Spike 15: away players, and take
about Two against two, all bots: every player is away, their bot playing. At 2 minutes blue.0's player logs in, takes blue.1's units (BAR's /take: blue.1's shade turns blue.0's), and sends the whole army at red. 4 minutes at 8x.

scenario economy
players blue 2
players red 2
clip 0..7200
speed 8
camera 256,256 400

at 3600 bot blue.0 off             # blue.0's player logs in: their bot stands down
at 3602 take blue.0
at 3604 select blue.0 tank as tanks
at 3604 select blue.0 raider as raiders
at 3604 select blue.0 artillery as guns
at 3606 attack-move tanks 440,256
at 3606 attack-move raiders 440,256
at 3606 attack-move guns 420,256

# Observed: just before, blue.1's bot has 23 units and blue.0's 27; after
# the take, blue.0 has all 50 and blue.1 none (its bot has nothing left to
# play). The army goes at red, which loses 60 by the end.
at 3599 expect blue.1 units >= 15
at 3604 expect blue.1 units == 0
at 3604 expect blue.0 units >= 40
at 7200 expect blue.1 units == 0
at 7200 expect red lost >= 30
